  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tAccounts Production\n\t\tCommunity Interest Companies (CIC)\n\n### Converting an existing client to a CIC\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Mon, 17 Aug, 2026 at  2:25 PM\n\n\t\tThis article explains how to convert an existing limited company client to a Community Interest Company (CIC) in Capium, rather than creating a new client. It also covers the client information fields worth reviewing at this stage and why completing them matters for later modules.\n\nNote: If you are setting up a brand new client as a CIC rather than converting an existing one, refer to this article.\n### Before you start\n\nThe client must currently be set up in Capium as a Limited company type. Only limited company clients can be converted to a CIC.\nYou will need access to the My Admin module.\nReview the client's existing record before you start, so you can identify any of the fields below that are missing or out of date.\n\n### Converting the client\n\nNavigate to the client section and select the client. Navigation > My Admin > Clients > Select Client\nConfirm the client type is set to Limited company. \nSelect the option to designate the client as a CIC. \nReview and update the client's details. \nSave the client record.\n\n### Option 2: converting via Accounts Production report settings\n\nYou can also convert a client to a CIC from within Accounts Production, at the point where you are setting up the client's report settings. This is useful if you are already working on the client's accounts and want to enable CIC status without leaving Accounts Production.\n\nNavigate to the client's report settings. Navigation > Accounts Production > Select Client > Settings > Report Settings > Company Info\nSelect Edit at the bottom of the screen to make changes. \nEnable the option for the company being a CIC. \nConfirm and save your changes.\n\nImportant: Enabling CIC status from this screen automatically creates the CIC 34 notes for the client. You will need to go on and complete these notes, which is covered in Accounts Production: report settings and CIC 34 notes for CIC clients.\n\nRelated Articles:\n\nCIC Accounts Walkthrough\nCIC Filings in Accounts Production\nHow to generate and file the CIC accounts and CIC 34 report\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
  "bodyHtml": "\n\t<div class=\"breadcrumb\">\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions\"> Solution home </a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/9000115345\">Accounts Production</a>\n\t\t<a href=\"/support/solutions/folders/9000202818\">Community Interest Companies (CIC)</a>\n\t</div>\n\t<b class=\"page-stamp page-stamp-article\">\n\t\t<b class=\"icon-page-article\"></b>\n\t</b>\n\n\t<h2 class=\"heading\">Converting an existing client to a CIC\n\t \t<a href=\"#\"\n            class=\"solution-print--icon print--remove\"\n \t\t\ttitle=\"Print this Article\"\n \t\t\tarial-role=\"link\"\n \t\t\tarial-label=\"Print this Article\"\n\t\t\tid=\"print-article\"\n \t\t>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"icon-print\"></span>\n\t\t\t<span class=\"text-print\">Print</span>\n \t\t</a>\n\t</h2>\n\t\n\t<p>Modified on: Mon, 17 Aug, 2026 at  2:25 PM</p>\n\t<hr />\n\t\n\n\t<article class=\"article-body\" id=\"article-body\" rel=\"image-enlarge\">\n\t\t<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\" data-sourcepos=\"17:1-17:282;603-884\" dir=\"ltr\"><span dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\">This article explains how to convert an existing limited company client to a Community Interest Company (CIC) in Capium, rather than creating a new client. It also covers the client information fields worth reviewing at this stage and why completing them matters for later modules.</span><span style=\"font-size: 14px;\"><span style=\"font-family: Verdana,Geneva,sans-serif;\"><br></span></span></p><div class=\"overflow-x-auto w-full px-2 mb-6 print:overflow-x-visible\" data-sourcepos=\"19:1-20:8;886-1077\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;\"><table class=\"min-w-full border-collapse text-sm leading-[1.7] whitespace-normal\"><thead class=\"text-left\"><tr><th class=\"text-text-100 border-b-0.5 border-[hsl(var(--border-300)/0.6)] py-2 pr-4 align-top font-bold\" scope=\"col\" style=\"font-size: 14px; background-colo